<title>NETHERLANDS: Ryder shows interest in take-over of KLM's KES.</title>
<headline>Ryder shows interest in take-over of KLM's KES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Ryder PLC has expressed interest in taking over KES, KLM Equipment Services BV, a 100 percent subsidiary of KLM Royal Dutch Airlines.</p>
<p>KES specialises in the maintenance, management and renting of airport ground equipment. The company operates independently from KLM, a KLM spokesman said.</p>
<p>At the moment its activities are centred on the Netherlands, said the spokesman.</p>
<p>KES employs around 180 people.</p>
<p>Ryder's parent company is Ryder Systems Inc. of Miami in the U.S.</p>
<p>A decision on the possible take-over deal is expected in the next few weeks. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
